    "blurb": "Teams and Slack process notifications",
    "overview": "Send messages, Adaptive Cards, Block Kit payloads, and Camunda forms to Microsoft Teams and Slack from your BPMN processes. Create channels and run chat-driven, human-in-the-loop processes, with no bot tokens or app credentials to manage in your process models.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Bring your processes into Microsoft Teams and Slack",
    "splashDescription": "The App Integrations connector lets your Camunda processes talk to people where they already work: Microsoft Teams and Slack. Send plain-text messages to channels, people, and existing conversations, or to the Camunda users and groups responsible for a task, and add richer content, including a Camunda form that collects input right in the chat. Your process learns which destinations each message reached and which failed, so it can follow up in the same conversation or react to a partial delivery. Create channels as part of a process, start a process when someone writes to the Camunda app, and wait for their reply to build chat-driven, human-in-the-loop processes. Because app integrations are configured once for your environment, there are no bot tokens or app credentials to manage in your process models.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/873768/overview/img6117275680291232980.png?d648d135d31f4c3a2a914a3c27929061",
